2026-05-01 23:12:52,583 subagents.hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] capabilities[fetch-current-month-orders] — The capability reads all orders for the current calendar month from the Shopify Admin API but describes no pagination loop. Shopify returns at most 250 orders per page, so any month with more than 250 orders will silently produce metrics computed on a truncated dataset — revenue, AOV, and repeat-customer count will all be understated with no error surfaced.
2026-05-01 23:12:52,584 subagents.hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[important] edgeCases[4] — The edge case claims concurrent refreshes are 'processed sequentially', but no serialization primitive (database advisory lock, queue, or idempotency key) is defined anywhere in the plan to enforce this. Without a mechanism, two concurrent POST requests will both read order data, both compute, and race on the upsert — the snapshot may reflect the earlier computation depending on commit order, contradicting the stated guarantee.
2026-05-01 23:12:52,584 subagents.hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[minor] externalContracts[0] GET /admin/metrics — The route always returns the current calendar month with no month_year query parameter in the requestShape, making it impossible for the admin UI to display or compare a prior month's snapshot without introducing a new endpoint or a breaking change to this one.
2026-05-01 23:12:52,584 subagents.hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[minor] externalContracts[0] GET /admin/metrics / edgeCases — The response shape includes a 'has_data' flag, implying a no-snapshot state (e.g., first load at the start of a new month) is anticipated, but no edge case describes what values the other fields carry when has_data is false — null, zero, or omitted — leaving the front-end rendering logic undefined for this scenario.
2026-05-01 23:12:52,584 subagents.hld_v_agent.agent INFO hld_v[minor] capabilities[compute-monthly-metrics] / persistence[monthly_metrics_snapshot].columns[repeat_customer_count] — The plan defines 'repeat customer count' as customers with more than one order within the current month only, but the quality brief describes 'repeat customers by email match' without a same-month restriction; a merchant may reasonably expect cross-month repeat customers, and the narrower definition will silently undercount in low-volume months.
